From: gogo <gogo@bluedynamics.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:43:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Cap the number of blobs that collide with each other

Under a request flood, thousands of blobs collide head-on in the middle,
slow each other down and pile up; the bigger the pile, the slower each
frame, and since the physics advances per frame, the slower it drains.

max_colliding_blobs: N lets only N blobs in flight collide with other
blobs. Every blob is still drawn and falls normally; the rest pass
through other blobs (and still hit the walls with bouncing on). The
cost is in finding nearby pairs for every shape, so layer-based
filtering didn't help; leaving overflow blobs out does. Simulated at
1500 blobs/s: ~20 ms -> ~2 ms physics per frame with a cap of 1500.

--fast now sets max_colliding_blobs: 1500 (unless configured), and the
10-second stats line shows Colliding[n].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013kYwHzrj5ef427USqzf3UF
