diff --git a/README b/README
index 514cd1a..27ed5ac 100644
--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@ Performance:
   roughly halves the physics cost; bounces are a few pixels less exact.
   physics_rate: 2 or 3 forces a fixed rate.
 
+  --fast also lets at most 1500 blobs collide with each other at a time
+  (max_colliding_blobs: N in the config). Every blob is still drawn and
+  falls normally; blobs beyond the limit pass through the others. Without a
+  limit, a flood of requests can pile up thousands of colliding blobs in the
+  middle of the screen, and the more pile up, the slower they drain.
+
   If that's not enough: blob_collisions: false stops blobs colliding with
   each other (near-zero physics cost; 'c' toggles it while running), and
   max_blobs: N caps the blobs in flight (requests over the cap are still
@@ -89,7 +95,7 @@ Installation instructions (Windows):
 
